  "notes": "USAGE:\nA medical term commonly encountered in hospital and clinic settings. Used both as a noun and as a suru verb ({抜糸|ばっし}する). Patients will typically hear this word when their doctor discusses the timeline for stitch removal after surgery or wound treatment.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {抜糸|ばっし}する (to remove stitches)\n- {抜糸|ばっし}の{日|ひ} (the day of stitch removal)\n- {抜糸|ばっし}{後|ご} (after stitch removal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {縫合|ほうごう}: suturing — the opposite procedure, sewing a wound shut\n- {抜釘|ばってい}: removal of surgical pins or screws",
